    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. some of these seem like pretty standard complaints, but i've heard people call most of these arguments \"NIMBYism\" or just say they aren't based on real data. from a professional planning perspective, are these concerns actually legitimate, or are they mostly just excuses to stop change?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
