      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "From a professional planning perspective, these concerns are overwhelmingly legitimate and must be treated with serious policy analysis rather than dismissal as \"NIMBYism.\" Undeserved supply of affordable housing and genuine capacity limits on local services like schools and fire stations are well-documented issues that require robust data before new development occurs. While historical \"not in my front yard\" bias exists in many areas, effective urban planning relies on transparently assessing actual infrastructure data to ensure equitable distribution of growth.",
